The correct fix is to split into two ordered sequential passes, not double-buffer. First pass computes all `a` values (which don't feed back into the same sweep), then second pass computes all `b` values (which do feed from the first pass):

```cpp
for (int nl = 0; nl < R; nl++) {
    // Pass 1: Compute all a[i] (no dependencies within this pass)
    for (int i = 1; i < LEN_1D-1; i++) {
        a[i] = b[i-1] + c[i];
    }
    // Pass 2: Compute all b[i] (all read from newly computed a, not carried within)
    for (int i = 1; i < LEN_1D-1; i++) {
        b[i] = a[i+1] * d[i];
    }
    pb_mix(nl);
}
```

